de the way self-service does?\nThe self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Search by employee ID. Confirm the account status badge shows Locked before continuing \\u2014 do not reset a password on an account that isn't actually locked without further checks.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"This step is classified as a `tool_call` because the `solandra` platform provides an exact function match (`search_user`) for the SOP's instruction to 'Search by employee ID' (Gate 1). The platform is active (Gate 2), and the tool's ability to return user status directly aligns with the need to 'Confirm the account status badge shows Locked' (Gate 3). The required `employee_id` parameter is available as a `required_entity` (Gate 4).\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{{{entities.employee_id}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Ask the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"to